--
The GCC `__integer_pack` builtin with a CAST argument, as libstdc++ writes
std::make_integer_sequence (`integer_sequence<T, __integer_pack(T(N))...>`).
With the `T(N)` cast the pack-expansion argument is stored as an `ambiguous`
function type (vexing parse: `code` returning `__integer_pack`, parameter `T N`),
so the plain-call __integer_pack expansion missed it.  Fixed by also recognising
that shape (count = parameter name N, element type = parameter type T), greening
deduction from the real std::make_index_sequence (this test uses both a
hand-written cast alias and the real std::make_index_sequence).  GCC-only builtin
(Clang uses __make_integer_seq).  Non-vacuous: each assertion is a concrete
function of the generated pack.
